Run the finish-launching callback right after finishLaunching

This change applies to zed-industries/zed 90d8514059561f0e44af0a32e84e1c329cef3232
after patches/0001 and patches/0002.

What it does:
- Call NSApplication.finishLaunching and run the app's finish-launching
  callback before app.run(), instead of waiting for LaunchServices'
  open-application Apple Event (~35ms idle on an M4).
- `run` skips finishLaunching when it has already happened; the
  delegate's did_finish_launching still installs observers when the
  event lands and finds no callback left to run.

Applied cleanly onto 90d8514 after 0001 and 0002. #64969's accessory
activation policy still runs before finishLaunching; Regular is still
applied in did_finish_launching. #65059's screen-parameters observer
and #65058's keychain/thermal moves sit elsewhere in platform.rs and
were not in this hunk.

Re-apply on a roll: git apply --3way patches/0003-finish-launching-immediately.patch
---
diff --git a/src/platform.rs b/src/platform.rs
index f053856..2ac8e61 100644
--- a/src/platform.rs
+++ b/src/platform.rs
@@ -581,6 +581,19 @@ impl Platform for MacPlatform {
             (*app_delegate).set_ivar(MAC_PLATFORM_IVAR, self_ptr);
 
             let pool = NSAutoreleasePool::new(nil);
+            // Finish launching now and run the app's callback directly. Left
+            // to `run`, AppKit sends `applicationDidFinishLaunching:` only
+            // once LaunchServices' open-application Apple Event has arrived,
+            // which is ~35ms of idle main thread between `finishLaunching`
+            // and the first window on an M4. `run` skips `finishLaunching`
+            // when it has already happened; the delegate's
+            // `did_finish_launching` still installs its observers when the
+            // event lands, and finds no callback left to run.
+            app.finishLaunching();
+            let callback = self.0.lock().finish_launching.take();
+            if let Some(callback) = callback {
+                callback();
+            }
             app.run();
             pool.drain();
 
